- op: discuss  # 054f
  at: '2026-08-06T09:03:35Z'  # 054f
  by: agent  # 054f
  actor: jgstern_agent  # 054f
  clock: 4  # 054f
  nonce: 054f  # 054f
  message: "CLAUSE L2 MECHANISM LANDED, clause NOT yet satisfied - stating the difference rather than claiming closure. WI-joluk built the coverage gate: cfg.uncovered_call_lines reports the call sites in a function AST body that no recorded CFG statement covers, and _ddg_taint_reaches gains forfeit_refutation which downgrades a would-be False to None. Verified live BEFORE the change, on the current signature, with both controls passing: the walk returns False for a value whose sink use sits in an if-initializer the def/use extractor never saw (positive control with the use recorded returns True; barren control returns None). So the defect this item names reproduces on merged dev today. WHY L2 IS NOT YET SATISFIED: the gate is built and tested but NOT WIRED - nothing in production passes forfeit_refutation=True, so a partially-recorded definition can still yield False in a real run. Closure requires the wiring plus a finding-delta measurement, and per this project closure-evidence discipline that means re-running THIS item own repro on the production path, not citing the unit test. NOTE ON THE FILED REPRO: it no longer runs as written. It passes ddg_uses keyed (symbol_id, line) and omits defs_at entirely; since PR #203 the key is (symbol_id, variable, def_line) and seeding comes from defs_at, so the filed call returns None for the wrong reason - my first reconstruction returned None for all three cases INCLUDING the positive control, i.e. the probe never reached the walk. Anyone re-running this must seed via defs_at. The faithful repro is: defs_at={(f,1):{v}}, ddg_uses={(f,v,1):{2}}, callees_at={(f,2):{fmt.Printf}} with production summaries, source_lines=[1], sink_lines=[5] -> returns False, true answer True. FORFEIT SHARE, which decides whether the gate is worth wiring: 12.8% to 35.5% across five repo-language pairs (details on WI-joluk). Not near 100%, so refutation stays viable on the remainder."  # 054f
- op: discuss  # 27a8
  at: '2026-08-08T21:03:20Z'  # 27a8
  by: agent  # 27a8
  actor: jgstern_agent  # 27a8
  clock: 5  # 27a8
  nonce: 27a8  # 27a8
  message: "L1 AND L3 ARE CLOSED WITH BEHAVIOURAL EVIDENCE. L2 IS STILL LIVE. Item stays\nviolated on L2 alone.\n\nLive probes against production _ddg_taint_reaches, all controls passing (earned\nFalse via fmt.Printf -> False; earned False via closed cycle -> False; earned\nTrue -> True):\n  L1 barren definition: this item's own filed repro `f,[1],[9],{}` -> None.\n     A barren seed beside a closed chain -> None. CLOSED (PR #199).\n  L3 (WI-votom dual-role statement): uncatalogued beside-call -> None,\n     catalogued-terminating -> False. CLOSED.\n  L2 partially-recorded definition (the item's own faithful repro):\n     gate OFF -> False; gate ON -> None; control with the use recorded -> True.\n     STILL LIVE.\n\nWHY L2 IS STILL LIVE, precisely: WI-joluk's `forfeit_refutation` IS wired\n(2edbc6a2c1) but ONLY to the barrier arm (taint.py:2792). The §3a arm\n(taint.py:~2735) passes nothing, so a partially-recorded definition still\nreturns False there.\n\nBLAST RADIUS TODAY IS ZERO, and wiring forfeit into the §3a arm today is a\nNO-OP: that arm tests `is True`, so False -> None changes nothing. 0 of 68\nproduction §3a walks return False at all. If §3a ever gains removal authority\nthe gate would forfeit 29/31 pretix walked functions (93.5%) and 1/1 mitmproxy.\n\nTHEREFORE: do NOT spend a cycle wiring it now. Land the §3a-arm forfeit IN THE\nSAME PR as any §3a removal authority -- PR #214 makes each unearned False DELETE\na flow, so the ordering is load-bearing.\n\nSECOND RESIDUAL: cfg.uncovered_call_lines keys on CALL nodes only, so a def/use\nomission at a non-call construct is invisible to the gate. Read from cfg.py:1457,\nNOT measured.\n\nCLOSURE EVIDENCE THIS ITEM WILL NEED: a live repro on a REAL REPO where a\nbarrier walk returns False on a partially-recorded def and the gate flips it to\nNone. Fixtures do not close it -- both existing demonstrations of barrier-arm\nbehaviour are fixtures, and 0 production barrier walks have ever been observed."  # 27a8
- op: discuss  # 142e
  at: '2026-08-10T02:42:16Z'  # 142e
  by: agent  # 142e
  actor: jgstern_agent  # 142e
  clock: 6  # 142e
  nonce: 142e  # 142e
  message: "DESCRIPTION DE-STALED 2026-08-09. The thread (2026-08-08) is current and correct;\nthe DESCRIPTION had drifted from it in two ways that matter.\n\n1. THE DANGEROUS ONE. The description's MINIMUM FIX paragraph says the change is\n   'safe, and behaviour-neutral on output today because nothing acts on False'.\n   That has been FALSE since PR #214: the barrier arm earns `sanitized` on a\n   False and a sanitized flow is DROPPED from a claim's violation set. This item's\n   own thread says so ('PR #214 makes each unearned False DELETE a flow'), so the\n   description contradicted its own thread for days. Anyone acting on the\n   description would conclude an unearned False is harmless, which is exactly\n   backwards.\n\n2. THE MECHANISM PARAGRAPH DESCRIBES CODE THAT NO LONGER EXISTS IN THAT FORM. It\n   says the walk 'does uses = ddg_uses.get((symbol_id, line)) and, when empty,\n   continues WITHOUT setting escaped'. On merged dev that branch is\n   `if not uses:` at taint.py:2204 carrying `# pragma: no cover - unreachable`\n   plus a comment explaining WHY it is unreachable (every seed comes from defs_at,\n   every frontier append is membership-tested first). The key is also\n   (symbol_id, variable, line) now, not (symbol_id, line).\n\n3. VERIFIED TODAY, and it agrees with the 2026-08-08 entry rather than adding\n   anything: the item's own filed repro `_ddg_taint_reaches('f',[1],[9],{})`\n   returns None. L1 remains closed. L2 remains the live clause and the reason this\n   item is still violated.\n\nNOT AMENDING THE DESCRIPTION TEXT HERE, deliberately: unlike WI-joluk, this\ndescription is the ORIGINAL panel finding and its trace already carries an explicit\nin-thread correction ('that particular example was never evidence for it'). Rewriting\nit would erase the provenance of a finding whose framing history is itself\nload-bearing. This note is the pointer. If a future reader disagrees, amend it -- but\namend the two sentences above first, in place, rather than adding a third banner."  # 142e
- op: discuss  # ca8d
