  nonce: ca8d  # ca8d
  message: "S8 re-measurement 2026-08-10 (dev ecb954eb05), for L2's pricing rather than its closure.\n\nThe section 3a walk produced 70 escape paths on hypergumbo's own tree with a passing positive control (595,736 edges offered / 317,528 accepted / 29,301 callees_at / 171 escape events). L2's own shape -- a definition the DDG never recorded reading as an accounted-for False -- is bounded by source_undefined + definition_unrecorded, which together are 2 of 70 sites (2.9%), both comparison_operator.\n\nL2 remains OPEN and its closure is unchanged: WI-joluk's coverage gate IS BUILT (cfg.uncovered_call_lines, forfeit_refutation) and wired to the BARRIER arm only. The section 3a arm is unwired DELIBERATELY, because wiring alone is a no-op and must land in the same PR as the removal authority it guards. Nothing in this measurement changes that sequencing.\n\nRecorded because the WI-vanun parked-adjudication trigger cites 'INV-lupav L2/L3 closed' as a condition, and that condition was re-checked here rather than inherited. Its stated reason there ('WI-joluk is todo_hard and unstarted') is STALE -- the gate exists -- but the trigger correctly has NOT fired."  # ca8d
- op: discuss  # 932c
  at: '2026-08-13T09:42:36Z'  # 932c
  by: agent  # 932c
  actor: jgstern_agent  # 932c
  clock: 8  # 932c
  nonce: 932c  # 932c
  message: "SECOND RESIDUAL MEASURED (full detail and instrument caveats on WI-joluk's thread, recorded there because the gate is WI-joluk's artifact; this is the L2-relevant summary).\n\nThe residual both items carry -- 'cfg.uncovered_call_lines keys on CALL nodes only, so a def/use omission at a NON-call construct is invisible to the gate' -- is now measured on two languages, using production's own registered def/use extractors as the classifier:\n\n    hypergumbo / python   GATE BLIND 31.9%   (positive control 33.7%, denominator 1,398)\n    alertmanager / go     GATE BLIND  3.1%   (positive control 20.3%, denominator 1,497)\n    prometheus / go       GATE BLIND  7.8%   (positive control 17.5%, denominator 5,014)\n\nGATE BLIND = the function holds a definition no recorded CFG statement carries, AND uncovered_call_lines returns empty so refutation is still permitted. That is THIS ITEM'S L2 SHAPE surviving the gate built to stop it.\n\nDirect demonstration rather than an aggregate:\n\n    def handler(items, flag):\n        total = 0\n        for item in items:      <- binds item\n            total += item       <- USES item\n        with open('f') as fh:   <- binds fh\n            data = fh.read()    <- USES fh\n        return total, data\n\nThe CFG records six statements and holds definitions for exactly {total, data}. Neither construct necessarily contains a call, so the gate does not forfeit.\n\nLOWER BOUND: fh is not counted, because the extractor does not report the with-as target as a definition either -- a function whose only unrecorded binding is a context-manager target scores CLEAN.\n\nWHAT THIS DOES NOT CHANGE. L2 is still OPEN and its closure path is unchanged. The section 3a arm still tests 'is True' -- re-verified in code today at taint.py:2953, against the barrier arm's 'is False' at taint.py:3009 -- so wiring forfeit there is still a no-op that must land with WI-kabif's removal authority, which is out of scope by owner ruling. This measurement does not make L2 actionable and is not closure evidence.\n\nWHAT IT DOES CHANGE. It prices the gate for the moment removal authority IS granted. The forfeit share (12.8-35.5%) said the gate WOULD do work; this says how much it would MISS -- on python roughly a third of walkable functions would be permitted to refute while holding a definition the DDG never recorded. The dominant constructs are DISJOINT between languages (python for_statement/for_in_clause; go short_var_declaration), the same split the forfeit-share measurement found independently, which is again the argument against a per-language gap list."  # 932c
- op: discuss  # 8a7a
  at: '2026-08-17T00:18:52Z'  # 8a7a
  by: agent  # 8a7a
  actor: jgstern_agent  # 8a7a
  clock: 9  # 8a7a
  nonce: 8a7a  # 8a7a
  message: "L2 RE-VERIFIED AND RE-PRICED 2026-08-16 (dev 80bbba4be7). Status stays violated\non L2. One claim carried by this item's own thread is REFUTED below.\n\n1. L2 STILL REPRODUCES, on the faithful (defs_at-seeded) repro, live at tip:\n     partially-recorded def, gate OFF -> False      <- the defect\n     same, forfeit_refutation=True   -> None        <- the gate answers it\n     positive control (use at sink line recorded) -> True\n     barren control (L1, PR #199)                 -> None\n   So the mechanism is unchanged and L1 remains closed.\n\n2. THE PRICING WAS RE-MEASURED RATHER THAN INHERITED, because the 2026-08-08\n   numbers predate INV-zuhig (08-16), which put dispatches_to into\n   TAINT_CALL_EDGE_TYPES, made all 8 dispatch linkers taint-visible, and took\n   sanitizer-credited flows 0 -> 98. That is a substrate change to exactly the\n   population this item counts. Instrument: production _ddg_taint_reaches\n   wrapped, every call tallied by arm and verdict, over real verify-claims runs.\n\n     hypergumbo, own claims file, rc 3   51 walks   51 s3a / 0 barrier / 0 False\n     alertmanager, Go, probe catalogue   34 walks   34 s3a / 0 barrier / 0 False\n\n   ACROSS BOTH: the walk returned False ZERO times in 85 production calls.\n   The s3a arm's inertness therefore holds for a reason stronger than the one\n   filed: not merely that its False is collapsed by the is-True test, but that\n   no production walk has been observed to produce a False at all.\n\n3. REFUTED: \"0 production barrier walks have ever been observed\" (2026-08-08\n   entry on this thread; INV-busis carries the same claim in its live\n   root_cause field, itemised as \"alertmanager 3/3/0\"). The barrier arm runs.\n   A/B on ONE repo and ONE binary, changing ONE variable:\n\n     alertmanager, no sanitizer for the flow label     34 walks,  0 barrier\n     alertmanager, + 9 laundering fns as sanitizers    55 walks, 21 barrier\n                                                       (11 True, 1 None ungated;\n                                                        6 True, 3 None gated)\n\n   BARRIER-ARM REACHABILITY IS A PROPERTY OF THE SANITIZER CATALOGUE, NOT OF\n   THE CODE. The built-in sanitizer catalogue expresses exactly two transforms\n   (plaintext -> ciphertext, key_material -> derived_key), so a flow under any\n   other label CANNOT be reported sanitized and the arm is unreachable by\n   construction. Every prior measurement ran under that near-empty default and\n   generalised \"0 barrier walks on every measured repo\". The correct population\n   was \"repos analysed with the default sanitizer catalogue\". A project that\n   declares its own sanitizers -- which is what --taint-sanitizers and\n   extra_catalogs exist for, and what hypergumbo's own claims file does -- lands\n   on the arm immediately. The 9 probe sanitizers were ordinary laundering\n   functions (net/url.QueryEscape, html.EscapeString, path/filepath.Clean,\n   strings.TrimSpace, ...), not a contrived shape.\n\n4. THE GATE PREVENTED 0 SUPPRESSIONS. Counterfactual re-run of every gated\n   barrier walk with the gate forced off: no walk changed False -> None,\n   because none returned False. 9 of 21 barrier walks (43%) had the gate ON,\n   consistent with the 12.8-35.5% forfeit share on WI-joluk.\n\n5. WHY False IS NEVER SEEN, and it is INV-busis's finding from the other side:\n   False requires the walk to EXHAUST with every step accounted for, and\n   escapes dominate (INV-busis measures 66.7-90.6% of blocked-walk sites as\n   non-calls). So values reach (True) or escape (None); exhaustion is the rare\n   third outcome. INV-busis says \"s3a cannot refute\"; L2 says \"when it does\n   refute, the refutation may be unearned\". Same fact, two faces. L2's\n   production population is 0 MEASURED -- not 0 by construction.\n\n6. SEQUENCING UNCHANGED, AND NOW ENFORCED RATHER THAN NOTED. The instruction\n   \"do not wire the s3a forfeit now; land it in the SAME PR as any s3a removal\n   authority\" is re-confirmed correct: s3a's result feeds only\n   adjudicated = (walk is True), whose sole consequence is the finding's\n   confidence/analysis_method label, so False -> None is observably nothing and\n   cannot carry a behavioural test. That instruction lived only in this thread\n   and a source comment. It is now a structural guard:\n   packages/hypergumbo-core/tests/test_taint_refutation_gate_contract.py\n   fails if either arm consumes the walk's False without passing\n   forfeit_refutation, and carries its own positive controls so it cannot pass\n   vacuously (the failure mode of the retired test_barren_seed_line_is_skipped).\n\nLIMITS, STATED: two repos, two languages, one synthetic-but-realistic sanitizer\ncatalogue. I did not measure how often real projects declare a same-function\nsanitizer, so item 3 establishes REACHABILITY, not prevalence."  # 8a7a
