  message: "P0/P1 SWEEP 2026-08-17, dev 11a240f83d. Every claim below was re-derived against the current tree, not re-read off this thread.\n\nRE-VERIFIED AT TIP, INDEPENDENTLY, WITH THE CONTROL PASSING. Status stays violated on L2. Run against dev 11a240f83d:\n\n    positive control (use at sink line recorded)   -> True   ADMISSIBLE\n    L1 filed repro  _ddg_taint_reaches(f,[1],[9],{}) -> None   CLOSED (was False)\n    L2 partially-recorded def, gate OFF            -> False  STILL VIOLATED\n    L2 same, forfeit_refutation=True               -> None   gate answers it\n\nThe control is printed first and decides admissibility, because the trap recorded on WI-joluk -- a reconstruction omitting callees_at/summaries returns None in EVERY arm including the control, so the probe never reached the walk -- has now caught two attempts. It did not catch a third.\n\nDESCRIPTION EDITED, not annotated. The description opened with 'VERIFIED LIVE DEFECT ... _ddg_taint_reaches(\"f\", [1], [9], {}) -> False', which is the L1 clause PR #199 closed on 2026-08-04 and which the run above shows returns None. A reader arriving at this P0 met a refuted repro as the first thing on the item. Per the excise-don't-banner rule the opening is now the L2 repro that does reproduce, with L1 recorded as closed; the mechanism, the cfg_nodes/go.yaml self-documented gap and the coverage-gate remedy are unchanged."  # 0b0b
