  message: "PRIORITY CHANGED 2026-08-17, on owner authorisation, as part of the P0/P1 sweep. Recording the reasoning here because a re-rank that lives only in conversation is indistinguishable next session from drift.\n\nTHE GATE. This item terminates at WI-kabif's removal authority, which is parked TWICE OVER: (1) a standing owner ruling of DO NOT START, and (2) a pre-registered numeric threshold -- measurement 0001 records that the removal-authority question becomes \"arguable on its merits\" near 80% precision, and states that no reading of the data supports a number near 80% (measured ~41%). So this is parked on a NUMBER, not on effort, and no amount of session time moves it.\n\nP0 -> P2. This was the tracker's ONLY P0 and sat at RANK 1 of 227 in tracker ready with no dependency edges, so every session picked it up first. Two facts make that ranking wrong:\n\n  1. IT CANNOT BE WORKED. The remaining clause is L2, and closing it means wiring the section 3a arm -- which this item's own thread, WI-joluk's description, and test_taint_refutation_gate_contract.py all say must land in the SAME PR as WI-kabif's removal authority. Wiring it alone is a measured no-op (the 3a arm tests `is True`, so False and None collapse).\n  2. IT CHANGES NOTHING TODAY. Across 85 production walks on two repos and two languages the walk returned False ZERO times.\n\nNOT A DOWNGRADE OF THE DEFECT. L2 re-reproduced at tip on 2026-08-17 with the positive control passing, and since PR #214 an unearned False DELETES a flow. The severity is unchanged; what changes is the claim that a session should work this before anything else. The tracker now has no P0, which is the honest reading: nothing is currently both critical and actionable."  # f5cc
