  message: "PHASE 0 RE-VERIFICATION AT TIP, 2026-08-25, dev e41a655d6d. L2 STILL\nREPRODUCES AT THE UNIT LEVEL -- and is NOT a live fail-open on published\noutput. Both halves matter; the second is why this item leaves the campaign's\nPhase 1.\n\nTHE FILED REPRO, control printed first and admissible:\n    positive control (use at sink line recorded) -> True   ADMISSIBLE\n    L1 filed repro _ddg_taint_reaches(f,[1],[9],{}) -> None   (closed, PR #199)\n    L2 partially-recorded def, gate OFF          -> False  <- the defect\n    L2 same, forfeit_refutation=True             -> None\nIdentical to the 2026-08-17 sweep. Status stays violated.\n\nBUT False HAS EXACTLY TWO CONSUMERS AND NEITHER IS EXPOSED.\n  taint.py:3326 (section 3a arm) tests `is True`, so False and None collapse.\n  taint.py:3378 (barrier arm) DOES pass forfeit_refutation.\n\nAND THE COVERAGE PREDICATE FIRES ON THE MOTIVATING CONSTRUCT. Measured on a Go\nfixture carrying this item's own caddy shape, with a control in the same run:\n\n    ddg_symbols   : ['go:main.go:16-20:covered:function',\n                     'go:main.go:8-14:leak:function']\n    forfeit_refut : ['go:main.go:8-14:leak:function']   <- if-initializer, FORFEITED\n    edges         : leak    1  (cwd->msg only; msg's use never recorded)\n                    covered 2  (fully recorded)         <- CONTROL, not forfeited\n\nSo WI-joluk's gate catches exactly the class this item was filed for, and it\nis not vacuously forfeiting everything.\n\nCONSEQUENCE FOR THE CAMPAIGN. This item is correctly filed and correctly\nparked: closing L2 means wiring the section 3a arm, which this thread,\nWI-joluk and test_taint_refutation_gate_contract.py all say must land in the\nSAME PR as WI-kabif's removal authority -- and WI-kabif is parked on a NUMBER\n(measurement 0001 ~41% vs the ~80% at which removal authority becomes\narguable). Removed from the campaign's Phase 1 fail-open family; it is not\nproducing a false all-clear today. Not a downgrade of the defect."  # dc2f
